Recent studies have provided precise measurements of $B 	o D^{(*)} 	au  ar{
u}$ decays, offering new insight and validating $q 	o q' 	au  ar{
u}$ semi-leptonic processes beyond the Standard Model such as the $U_1$ leptoquark model. This paper delves into the impact of $B_{,D^{(*)}} 	o D^{(*)}$ data on the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ process within the $U_1$ leptoquark model, addressing it at both tree and one-loop levels. By leveraging a perturbative QCD approach, we estimate branching ratios and forward-backward asymmetries for $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$, and incorporate $B 	o D^{(*)} 	au  ar{
u}$ measurements to constrain form factors for $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$. This results in predicted values for $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ that differ significantly from initial predictions, with the forward-backward asymmetry remaining positive, in contrast to $SM$ expectations.
